{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"characterDiffThreshold","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Discussion","type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The default value is ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Pass ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" to disable collapsing.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"When comparing strings, if the percentage of changed characters exceeds","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"this threshold, a string-to-string diff is performed instead of a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"character-by-character diff. For example, a threshold of ","type":"text"},{"code":"0.75","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" would","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"collapse diffs where more than 75% of characters changed.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"This is useful for avoiding noisy diff output when comparing unrelated","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"or significantly different strings, while preserving granular diffs for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"typos and small changes.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Consider the situation in which the expected string ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"12345\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"compared to the actual string ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"54321\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". 80% of the characters are","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"considered to have changed, since only one of the five expected","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"characters (","type":"text"},{"code":"\"5\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") is present and in the correct position.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If collapsing is disabled, a character-by-character diff is performed.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Specifically, the diff would report the following:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The leading ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"1234\""},{"text":" in the expected string is missing.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"5\""},{"text":" in the expected string is present and unchanged.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The actual string has an unexpected trailing ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"\"4321\""},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"On the other hand, if collapsing is enabled and set to 75%, a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"string-to-string diff is performed instead, since 80% exceeds the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"threshold. The diff would simply indicate that the expected string","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"12345\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is not equal to the actual string ","type":"text"},{"code":"\"54321\"","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/TestKitCore\/documentation\/TestKitCore","doc:\/\/TestKitCore\/documentation\/TestKitCore\/DiffOptions"]]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/testkitcore\/diffoptions\/characterdiffthreshold"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"The threshold for collapsing character-level diffs.","type":"text"}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/TestKitCore\/documentation\/TestKitCore\/DiffOptions\/characterDiffThreshold","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"property","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"characterDiffThreshold","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","text":"Double","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"title":"characterDiffThreshold","externalID":"s:11TestKitCore11DiffOptionsV09characterD9ThresholdSdSgvp","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"SwiftTestKit and XCTestKit Core"}],"roleHeading":"Instance Property"},"references":{"doc://TestKitCore/documentation/TestKitCore/DiffOptions/characterDiffThreshold":{"title":"characterDiffThreshold","abstract":[{"text":"The threshold for collapsing character-level diffs.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/TestKitCore\/documentation\/TestKitCore\/DiffOptions\/characterDiffThreshold","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"characterDiffThreshold"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/testkitcore\/diffoptions\/characterdiffthreshold","role":"symbol"},"doc://TestKitCore/documentation/TestKitCore":{"type":"topic","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/TestKitCore\/documentation\/TestKitCore","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/testkitcore","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Core types shared by SwiftTestKit and XCTestKit."}],"title":"SwiftTestKit and XCTestKit Core"},"doc://TestKitCore/documentation/TestKitCore/DiffOptions":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TestKitCore\/documentation\/TestKitCore\/DiffOptions","type":"topic","title":"DiffOptions","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DiffOptions"}],"url":"\/documentation\/testkitcore\/diffoptions","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DiffOptions","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The options for computing diffs.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol"}}}